Document Structure: ASR Smart Tiering Standard Operating Procedure
1. Executive Summary & Architecture Overview

Concept: What ASR Smart Tiering is (decoupling target storage from production storage).

Business Value: Financial impact and elimination of dormant provisioned capacity waste.

Safety Guarantee: Why this has zero impact on active production workloads and RPO/RTO.

2. Prerequisites & Security Setup

Automation Account: Location requirements (Target DR Region / Same Subscription as Recovery Vault).

RBAC / Permissions: Setup of the System Assigned Managed Identity and the Virtual Machine Contributor role assignment on the target Resource Group.

3. Integration: Automating the Failover (The Runbook)

Script Deployment: Importing the PowerShell runbook.

Recovery Plan Configuration: Adding the script to the Group 1: Post-steps phase to ensure VMs are powered off, upgraded to Premium SSD, and rebooted during a DR event.

4. Operations: Retrofitting Existing ASR Replicas

This will detail the exact click-ops process for the Prod team to downgrade current disks.

Method: Navigating to the Recovery Vault > Target VM > Re-configuring replication settings (or canceling the SAS export lock) to switch the passive disks from Premium SSD to Standard HDD.

5. Operations: Executing a DR Test & Validation

Initiating the Drill: Running a Test Failover.

Expected Behavior: The cold boot phenomenon, application cache hydration, and total time to execution.

Validation: How the Prod team verifies the disks successfully upgraded to Premium SSD in the target region.

6. Operations: Cleanup & Failback

Test Cleanup: Purging the DR environment post-test.

Re-securing Storage: Ensuring the replication resumes smoothly on Standard HDDs.
